{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '839,940p;1168,1253p;1510,1545p' && nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '178,219p' && rg -n ':tail\\\\?|tail\\\\?' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/{stack,register}.cljc | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"   839\t;; The continuation lane (slice 5, ported off the outcome model)\n   840\t;; =============================================================================\n   841\t;;\n   842\t;; Opted in with `:outcomes true` beside the argument-vector convention (the\n   843\t;; flag now selects the continuation lane, not the retired outcome tuples).\n   844\t;; Guest functions return plain values; `throw` lowers to `clj/throw`, `try`\n   845\t;; to `clj/try`/`clj/try-finally` (the `%capture` handler-stack family), and a\n   846\t;; guest call delivers an escaping condition through the §8.10.7 raise exit.\n   847\t;; The public entry installs the same bridge before argument binding. Only the\n   848\t;; `compile-program` boundary still wraps the program in `[:yin.k/ok value]` /\n   849\t;; `[:yin.k/error raised]` for the harness. `ex-info` becomes a portable map\n   850\t;; under namespaced keys, `ex-message`/`ex-data` its accessors. Generated names\n   851\t;; carry the reserved `dsg__` prefix; the program pre-pass keeps user code out\n   852\t;; of that prefix. A macro call is opaque to the pass: the expander owns it.\n   853\t\n   854\t(def ^:private ok-tag :yin.k/ok)\n   855\t\n   856\t(def ^:private error-tag :yin.k/error)\n   857\t\n   858\t\n   859\t(defn- outcomes?\n   860\t  [env]\n   861\t  (some? (::outcomes env)))\n   862\t\n   863\t\n   864\t(defn- rebuild\n   865\t  \"A list of `items` carrying the reader metadata of `form`.\"\n   866\t  [form items]\n   867\t  (let [out (apply list items)]\n   868\t    (if-let [m (meta form)]\n   869\t      (with-meta out m)\n   870\t      out)))\n   871\t\n   872\t\n   873\t;; =============================================================================\n   874\t;; The clj continuation family (R3 §8.10.7; the (B) port)\n   875\t;; =============================================================================\n   876\t;;\n   877\t;; The port converges clojure's exception lowering onto the continuation\n   878\t;; encoding: a `%capture` handler stack in a dynamic-context cell, exactly\n   879\t;; like the py/ts/php preludes (`yang.clojure.prelude` carries the reference\n   880\t;; implementation under `clj/`). A source `(throw e)` lowers to `clj/throw`,\n   881\t;; `(try ...)` to `clj/try`/`clj/try-finally`, and function bodies return\n   882\t;; plain values. A guest call delivers a callee's escaping condition through\n   883\t;; the §8.10.7 raise exit, and the public entry installs the same bridge.\n   884\t;; Ordinary thrown values remain raw; protocol conditions travel in a\n   885\t;; provenance carrier. `compile-program` emits this family\n   886\t;; inline (the linked runtime binds the same family from the prelude); it\n   887\t;; routes the capture-sensitive primitives through the `dsg__*` helpers so a\n   888\t;; program definition of `get`/`assoc`/`=` cannot capture a frame access.\n   889\t\n   890\t(def ^:private continuation-family\n   891\t  \"The `clj/` continuation family, `[key form]` in prelude notation (each\n   892\t   form is read with `u/sexp->uast`). Mirrors `yang.clojure.prelude`'s\n   893\t   escapes section, minus `call-ec`/`unwind-to` (clojure has no\n   894\t   break/continue/return escapes). The handler stack is a chain of frames\n   895\t   [tag payload rest n]; a `:handler` frame holds the continuation\n   896\t   `clj/raise` delivers to, a `:finally` frame a one-argument thunk every\n   897\t   exit through it runs.\"\n   898\t  '[[clj/ctx (fn [hs] (dsg__assoc {} :handlers hs))]\n   899\t    [clj/handlers (fn [] (dsg__get (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\n   900\t    [clj/set-handlers!\n   901\t     (fn [hs]\n   902\t       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (dsg__assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers hs)))]\n   903\t    [clj/restore! (fn [saved] (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx saved))]\n   904\t    [clj/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (dsg__equal hs nil) 0 (dsg__get hs 3)))]\n   905\t    [clj/frame\n   906\t     (fn [tag payload rest]\n   907\t       (conj (conj (conj (conj [] tag) payload) rest)\n   908\t             (+ 1 (clj/frame-depth rest))))]\n   909\t    [clj/pop-frame\n   910\t     (fn [hs]\n   911\t       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx\n   912\t                  (dsg__assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers (dsg__get hs 2))))]\n   913\t    [clj/raise\n   914\t     (fn [e]\n   915\t       (let [hs (clj/handlers)]\n   916\t         (if (dsg__equal hs nil)\n   917\t           (dsg__get e :clj/no-handler)\n   918\t           (if (dsg__equal (dsg__get hs 0) :finally)\n   919\t             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((dsg__get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n   920\t             ((dsg__get hs 1) e)))))]\n   921\t    [clj/throw (fn [e] (clj/raise e))]\n   922\t    [clj/try\n   923\t     (fn [body handler]\n   924\t       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)\n   925\t             flag (cell/new :first)]\n   926\t         ((fn [r]\n   927\t            (if (dsg__equal (cell/get flag) :first)\n   928\t              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n   929\t                  (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :handler r (dsg__get saved :handlers)))\n   930\t                  (let [v (body)] (do (clj/restore! saved) v)))\n   931\t              (do (clj/restore! saved) (handler r))))\n   932\t          (%capture))))]\n   933\t    [clj/try-finally\n   934\t     (fn [body fin]\n   935\t       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)]\n   936\t         (do (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :finally fin (dsg__get saved :handlers)))\n   937\t             (let [v (body)]\n   938\t               (do (clj/restore! saved) (fin nil) v)))))]])\n   939\t\n   940\t\n  1168\t(defn- outcome-node\n  1169\t  [tag value]\n  1170\t  (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/lit tag)) value))\n  1171\t\n  1172\t\n  1173\t(defn- call-entry\n  1174\t  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body. It\n  1175\t   installs the exception bridge (`clj/try`) before argument binding, so an\n  1176\t   escaping raise forwards an authenticated condition or wraps an ordinary\n  1177\t   value as `:yang.call/thrown` exactly once after cleanup.\"\n  1178\t  []\n  1179\t  (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"body\"))\n  1180\t        invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invocation\"))\n  1181\t        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n  1182\t        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n  1183\t        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n  1184\t        binding-error (u/app\n  1185\t                        (u/v 'clj/throw)\n  1186\t                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n  1187\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n  1188\t                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n  1189\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n  1190\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n  1191\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n  1192\t        forged-refusal (u/app\n  1193\t                         (u/v 'clj/throw)\n  1194\t                         (u/lit {:yin.k/message\n  1195\t                                 \"Invocation is neither an authenticated packet nor an invocation record\"\n  1196\t                                 :yin.k/data {}}))\n  1197\t        ;; The record path: bind and run the body under clj/try, delivering\n  1198\t        ;; an authenticated condition or a fresh :yang.call/thrown condition.\n  1199\t        entry-body (u/app\n  1200\t                     (u/v 'clj/try)\n  1201\t                  